IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc3-helpers`
IMPORT `ssc3-f-s55a-s56`

-- Tests for ssc3-f-s55a-s56.l4 (ss 55A, 55AA, 55B, 55C, 56).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the text of the section named beside it; none is copied from the encoding's output.
-- The fixtures' dates are chosen for the comparisons under test; a fixture is not a claim about when anyone really attains pensionable age (that is the keel's fact, ssc-core.l4).

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN `their sex` IS A Sex
      born IS A DATE
      attained IS A DATE
GIVETH A Person
`a person` MEANS
    Person WITH
        `date of birth` IS born
        `sex` IS `their sex`
        `marital status` IS `married`
        `date of attaining pensionable age` IS attained

`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012` MEANS `a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 1 1 2012)

§ `Section 55A: shared additional pension because of an old state scheme pension credit`

-- (7): the final relevant year is the tax year before the one in which the pensioner attains pensionable age. 1 January 2012 falls in 2011-12, so 2010-11.
#ASSERT (`s 55A(7) the final relevant year` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 1 1 2012)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2010
#ASSERT (`s 55A(7) the final relevant year` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 6 4 2012)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2011
#ASSERT (`s 55A(7) the final relevant year` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 5 4 2012)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2010
-- (7): "old state scheme pension credit" means a credit under section 49(1)(b).
#ASSERT `s 55A(7) the credit is an old state scheme pension credit` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55A(7) the credit is an old state scheme pension credit` FALSE))
-- (7): "valuation day" means the day the pensioner becomes entitled to the credit.
#ASSERT `s 55A(7) the valuation day` (Date 1 3 2005) EQUALS Date 1 3 2005
-- (1): entitled if the person attained pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and is entitled to an old state scheme pension credit.
#ASSERT `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 6 4 2016)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55A(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55A` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 6 4 2016)) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): the entitlement continues throughout life.
#ASSERT `s 55A(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55A is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2019) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55A(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55A is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2020) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55A(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55A is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55A(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55A is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 2 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) and (5): the appropriate weekly amount and the revaluation percentage arrive as inputs and are passed on.
#ASSERT `s 55A(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` (JUST 12.5) EQUALS JUST 12.5
#ASSERT `s 55A(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55A(5) the relevant revaluation percentage` (JUST 105) EQUALS JUST 105
#ASSERT `s 55A(5) the relevant revaluation percentage` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the pensioner attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012, so the final relevant year began on 6 April 2010. A credit that arose on 5 April 2010 arose before it: 20 x 110/100 = 22.
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 5 4 2010) (JUST 20) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 22
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 6 4 2010) (JUST 20) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 1 1 2011) (JUST 20) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 5 4 2010) (JUST 20) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 5 4 2010) NOTHING (JUST 110) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55A(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 6 4 2010) NOTHING (JUST 110) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 55AA: shared additional pension because of a new state scheme pension credit`

-- (4): "new state scheme pension credit" means a credit under section 49A(2)(b).
#ASSERT `s 55AA(4) the credit is a new state scheme pension credit` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55AA(4) the credit is a new state scheme pension credit` FALSE))
-- (1): entitled if the person reached pensionable age before 6 April 2016 and is entitled to a new state scheme pension credit.
#ASSERT `s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 6 4 2016)) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55AA(1) the person is entitled to a shared additional pension under section 55AA` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1956) (Date 5 4 2016)) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): the entitlement continues throughout life.
#ASSERT `s 55AA(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55AA is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2019) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55AA(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55AA is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2030) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55AA(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55AA is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55AA(2) the entitlement to the shared additional pension under section 55AA is running on the day` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 2 1 2025) (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the weekly rate is the amount of the credit.
#ASSERT `s 55AA(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` (JUST 30) EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `s 55AA(3) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 55B: reduction of shared additional pension: pension sharing`

-- (8): the final relevant year, as in section 55A(7).
#ASSERT (`s 55B(8) the final relevant year` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 1 1 2012)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2010
#ASSERT (`s 55B(8) the final relevant year` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1951) (Date 6 4 2012)))'s `calendar year in which it begins` EQUALS 2011
-- (8): "old state scheme pension debit" means a debit under section 49(1)(a); "valuation day" is the day the pensioner became subject to it.
#ASSERT `s 55B(8) the debit is an old state scheme pension debit` TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 55B(8) the debit is an old state scheme pension debit` FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 55B(8) the valuation day` (Date 1 3 2005) EQUALS Date 1 3 2005
-- (4) and (6): the appropriate weekly amount and the revaluation percentage arrive as inputs and are passed on.
#ASSERT `s 55B(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` (JUST 8) EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `s 55B(4) the appropriate weekly amount in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55B(6) the relevant revaluation percentage` (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 110
#ASSERT `s 55B(6) the relevant revaluation percentage` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the notional pension becomes payable on the later of attaining pensionable age (1 January 2012) and the valuation day.
#ASSERT `s 55B(5) the day the notional pension becomes payable` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS Date 1 1 2015
#ASSERT `s 55B(5) the day the notional pension becomes payable` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 1 1 2010) EQUALS Date 1 1 2012
#ASSERT `s 55B(5) the day the notional pension becomes payable` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) (Date 1 1 2012) EQUALS Date 1 1 2012
-- (2) and (3): the reduction is the appropriate weekly amount, or that amount multiplied by the revaluation percentage. 8 x 110/100 = 8.8.
#ASSERT `s 55B(2) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST 5) EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `s 55B(2) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55B(3) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 8.8
#ASSERT `s 55B(3) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` NOTHING (JUST 110) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55B(3) the reduction of the weekly rate in pounds` (JUST 8) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): the pensioner attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012, so the final relevant year began on 6 April 2010.
-- A debit on or after that day reduces a rate of 50 by the appropriate weekly amount 8, to 42; one before it by 8 x 110/100 = 8.8, to 41.2.
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 42
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2011) 50 (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 42
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 41.2
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) FALSE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE FALSE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) (JUST 110) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 (JUST 8) NOTHING EQUALS JUST 42
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) TRUE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 NOTHING (JUST 110) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55B(1) the weekly rate of the shared additional pension after the reduction in pounds` (`a woman who attained pensionable age on 1 January 2012`) FALSE TRUE (Date 6 4 2010) 50 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST 50

§ `Section 55C: pension increase or lump sum where entitlement to shared additional pension is deferred`

-- (1): Schedule 5A has effect where the entitlement is deferred.
#ASSERT `s 55C(1) Schedule 5A has effect` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55C(1) Schedule 5A has effect` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 55C(1) Schedule 5A has effect` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(a): where the person would be entitled to a Category A or B pension but for its deferment, deferred if and so long as that pension is.
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)(b): otherwise, if and so long as the person does not become entitled by reason only of not satisfying section 1 of the Administration Act.
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 55C(3) the shared additional pension is deferred` FALSE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 56: child's special allowance, existing beneficiaries`

-- (1): the weekly rate is that of Schedule 4, Part I, paragraph 6.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the weekly rate of the child's special allowance in pounds` (JUST 17.5) EQUALS JUST 17.5
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the weekly rate of the child's special allowance in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1): a divorced woman whose husband is dead and satisfied the contribution condition, who is entitled to child benefit, who (b) was entitled before his death, and (c) whose husband had been contributing to the child's cost.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1)(b): either she was entitled before his death or, in prescribed circumstances, he was.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1)(c): either the husband had been contributing, or she was entitled under an order to payments he provided.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): the marriage was terminated by divorce, the husband is dead, and the claimant is a woman.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Woman (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the woman is entitled to a child's special allowance` (`a person` Man (Date 1 1 1950) (Date 1 1 2010)) TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): not payable for any period after remarriage or while living together as husband and wife with a man not married to her.
#ASSERT `s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 56(2) payment of the child's special allowance is barred for the period` FALSE FALSE))
-- (5): the condition in (4)(b): contributions at not less than the amount (10) by the beneficiary, or by two spouses together, and (except in prescribed cases) over and above those needed for section 143(1)(b).
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 10 FALSE 0 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 9 FALSE 15 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 9 TRUE 10 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 9 TRUE 9 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 10 FALSE 0 10 (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 10 FALSE 0 10 (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 10 FALSE 0 10 NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 10 FALSE 0 10 (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(5) the condition in subsection (4)(b) is satisfied` 9 FALSE 0 10 NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): one of the two conditions.
#ASSERT `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(4) one of the conditions specified in subsection (4) is satisfied` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): where the person is otherwise entitled to receive payment, the amount is not payable unless one of the conditions is satisfied.
#ASSERT `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(3) payment of the amount is barred by subsection (3)` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6): for a day after 5 April 1987, payable only to a woman who immediately before 6 April 1987 satisfied (1)(a) to (c), was not barred under (2), and has so continued.
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 5 4 1987) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) NOTHING TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(6) payment of the child's special allowance for the day is barred by subsection (6)` (Date 6 4 1987) NOTHING TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6): payable when entitled under (1) and none of the bars holds.
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST FALSE) FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 56(1) the child's special allowance is payable to the woman for the day, subject to subsections (2), (3) and (6)` (JUST TRUE) FALSE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
